WEBVTT

1
00:00:16.106 --> 00:00:22.268
Cosette could not help casting one last look toward the beautiful doll displayed in the toy-shop stall.

2
00:00:22.849 --> 00:00:25.170
Then she knocked on the door of the inn.

3
00:00:26.030 --> 00:00:27.510
"Here you are at last!"

4
00:00:28.091 --> 00:00:30.692
said Madame Thenardier as she threw open the door.

5
00:00:31.388 --> 00:00:34.310
"You certainly took your time getting that water.

6
00:00:34.651 --> 00:00:36.392
What were you doing—playing?"

7
00:00:36.412 --> 00:00:42.716
"Madame," said Cosette, trembling, "here's a gentleman who needs a room."

8
00:00:43.577 --> 00:00:47.620
Madame Thenardier quickly replaced her fierce scowl with a friendly demeanor.

9
00:00:47.640 --> 00:00:49.201
"Come in, monsieur.

10
00:00:49.281 --> 00:00:57.948
Welcome!" As Jean Valjean stepped inside, she caught sight of his long, threadbare yellow coat and his tattered

11
00:00:58.008 --> 00:01:02.913
hat. His luggage consisted of a walking stick and a mysterious bundle.

12
00:01:03.493 --> 00:01:05.994
She glanced at her husband and wrinkled her nose.

13
00:01:06.794 --> 00:01:11.576
The innkeeper, who was sitting with some of the inn's guests, nodded in response.

14
00:01:13.856 --> 00:01:19.878
"Oh, I'm sorry, my good man," said Madame Thenardier, "but we have no rooms available."

15
00:01:19.898 --> 00:01:24.119
"Put me wherever you have space—in the garret, in the stable.

16
00:01:25.039 --> 00:01:27.180
I'll be happy to pay as if I had a regular room."

17
00:01:28.024 --> 00:01:30.766
"That'll be forty sous, paid in advance."

18
00:01:32.127 --> 00:01:32.948
"Forty sous?"

19
00:01:33.448 --> 00:01:35.870
whispered one of the guests to Monsieur Thenardier.

20
00:01:35.890 --> 00:01:38.131
"I thought a room was only twenty sous."

21
00:01:38.151 --> 00:01:42.194
"It's forty sous for him," replied the innkeeper.

22
00:01:42.214 --> 00:01:44.956
"We try to discourage guests like him.

23
00:01:45.316 --> 00:01:47.237
They ruin the inn's reputation."

24
00:01:48.258 --> 00:01:53.302
Meanwhile Valjean handed the cash to Madame Thenardier and took a seat at another table.

25
00:01:53.922 --> 00:01:58.930
Cosette quickly brought him something to drink and then took water to the guest's horse.

26
00:01:59.870 --> 00:02:06.075
When Cosette returned and resumed her place under the kitchen table with her knitting, Valjean couldn't take his

27
00:02:06.375 --> 00:02:07.075
eyes off her.

28
00:02:08.616 --> 00:02:14.921
This plain, thin little girl had dark circles under her eyes, which were dull from constant weeping.

29
00:02:15.842 --> 00:02:18.503
Her hands and bare legs were red and rough.

30
00:02:19.164 --> 00:02:22.646
Everything she wore was made of cotton and full of holes.

31
00:02:23.807 --> 00:02:28.353
She was shivering, so she drew up her knees and hugged them to her chest while she knit.

32
00:02:28.773 --> 00:02:33.635
Cosette was still wet from getting the water but didn't dare to warm herself by the fire.

33
00:02:34.695 --> 00:02:40.757
Fear made her take up the smallest possible space and prevented her from breathing more than necessary.

34
00:02:41.637 --> 00:02:44.558
Suddenly Madame Thenardier shouted, "Oh!

35
00:02:45.138 --> 00:02:46.118
Where is that bread?"

36
00:02:47.038 --> 00:02:52.360
Cosette, as she always did whenever Madame Thenardier raised her voice, sprang from under the table.

37
00:02:53.140 --> 00:02:57.503
The child had completely forgotten the bread, so she did the only thing she could think of.

38
00:02:58.143 --> 00:02:58.703
She lied.

39
00:02:58.723 --> 00:03:02.185
"Madame, the bakery was closed."

40
00:03:02.806 --> 00:03:04.226
"You should have knocked!"

41
00:03:04.246 --> 00:03:07.188
"I did, but no one answered."

42
00:03:07.208 --> 00:03:12.811
"I'll find out tomorrow if that's true, and if you're lying, you'll be in trouble.

43
00:03:13.532 --> 00:03:15.053
Give me the 15-sous coin."

44
00:03:15.913 --> 00:03:19.355
Cosette plunged her hand into her apron pocket and turned white.

45
00:03:19.815 --> 00:03:20.856
The coin was gone.

46
00:03:21.876 --> 00:03:24.857
She turned the pocket inside out, but there was still nothing.

47
00:03:25.377 --> 00:03:27.978
The poor girl was too frightened to utter a word.

48
00:03:27.998 --> 00:03:32.139
"Have you lost it or did you try to steal it from me?"

49
00:03:32.579 --> 00:03:33.999
screamed Madame Thenardier.

50
00:03:34.520 --> 00:03:37.140
She reached for a whip hanging near the fireplace.

51
00:03:37.160 --> 00:03:39.341
"Forgive me, madame!"

52
00:03:39.761 --> 00:03:40.501
cried Cosette.

53
00:03:41.041 --> 00:03:46.563
Watching this scene unfold, Valjean deftly removed a coin from his own waistcoat pocket.

54
00:03:47.723 --> 00:03:52.681
"I beg your pardon, madame," said Valjean, "but I just saw something fall out of the little girl's

55
00:03:52.741 --> 00:03:53.822
pocket and roll away."

56
00:03:54.862 --> 00:03:58.163
At the same time, he stooped down and appeared to search the floor.

57
00:03:58.183 --> 00:04:01.245
"Aha, here it is!"

58
00:04:01.725 --> 00:04:04.246
He handed Madame Thenardier a silver coin.

59
00:04:04.266 --> 00:04:07.147
"Yes, that's it."

60
00:04:07.928 --> 00:04:13.590
She put the coin in her own apron pocket and contented herself with giving Cosette a ferocious look

61
00:04:14.030 --> 00:04:17.252
and saying, "Don't ever let that happen again."

62
00:04:18.292 --> 00:04:21.035
Valjean's coin was actually a twenty-sous piece.

63
00:04:21.675 --> 00:04:25.498
That made up for the lack of bread as far as Madame Thenardier was concerned.

64
00:04:26.479 --> 00:04:29.822
A door now opened and Eponine and Azelma came in.

65
00:04:30.443 --> 00:04:34.426
They were so lively, neat, and plump that it was a pleasure to look at them.

66
00:04:35.247 --> 00:04:41.352
Madame Thenardier took them on her lap, one at a time, smoothing their hair and retying their hair

67
00:04:41.412 --> 00:04:44.555
ribbons. "What good girls they are!"

68
00:04:44.915 --> 00:04:45.416
she said.

69
00:04:46.004 --> 00:04:48.686
They went and sat by the fire and played with a doll.

70
00:04:49.447 --> 00:04:55.052
From time to time, Cosette raised her eyes from her knitting and looked sadly at them as they

71
00:04:55.092 --> 00:05:00.276
played. Eponine and Azelma paid no attention to Cosette.

72
00:05:00.796 --> 00:05:06.501
Their doll was old and faded, but it still seemed wonderful to Cosette, who had never had a

73
00:05:06.541 --> 00:05:12.886
doll. All of a sudden Madame Thenardier noticed that Cosette was watching the girls instead of knitting.

74
00:05:12.906 --> 00:05:15.008
"Is that how you work?"

75
00:05:15.408 --> 00:05:15.988
she cried.

76
00:05:16.008 --> 00:05:18.689
"I'll make you work with the whip, I will."

77
00:05:18.709 --> 00:05:21.310
"Oh, let her play," said Valjean.

78
00:05:22.270 --> 00:05:27.091
Now if a wealthy guest had made this request, Madame Thenardier might have agreed.

79
00:05:27.611 --> 00:05:30.252
But to hear such a thing from a pauper like this man!

80
00:05:30.272 --> 00:05:35.513
"She has to work in order to eat," snapped Madame Thenardier.

81
00:05:35.533 --> 00:05:38.474
"I don't support her so she can do nothing."

82
00:05:38.494 --> 00:05:40.275
"What's she making?"

83
00:05:40.295 --> 00:05:45.116
"Stockings for my girls, who have none to speak of and will soon be going barefoot."

84
00:05:46.612 --> 00:05:49.053
Valjean looked at Cosette's chapped red feet.

85
00:05:49.073 --> 00:05:51.634
"When will she be finished with a pair of stockings?"

86
00:05:51.654 --> 00:05:55.456
"It'll take her at least three or four days, the lazy thing."

87
00:05:55.476 --> 00:05:58.617
"If I pay you five francs, will you let her play?"

88
00:05:59.038 --> 00:05:59.778
asked Valjean.

89
00:06:00.318 --> 00:06:03.600
His offer was almost five times what the stockings were worth.

90
00:06:04.460 --> 00:06:08.982
Monsieur Thenardier decided to join the conversation now that Valjean was spending money.

91
00:06:09.002 --> 00:06:13.144
"If you want to pay that much for a pair of stockings, we can't refuse you."

92
00:06:14.064 --> 00:06:19.867
Valjean turned to Cosette and said, "Now your work belongs to me, and I say you should play."

93
00:06:20.928 --> 00:06:22.449
"Is it true, madame?"

94
00:06:22.869 --> 00:06:23.589
asked Cosette.

95
00:06:23.609 --> 00:06:25.290
"Can I really play?"

96
00:06:25.310 --> 00:06:29.813
"Play!" said Madame Thenardier in a terrible voice.

97
00:06:31.214 --> 00:06:34.095
Cosette did not move from her spot under the table.

98
00:06:34.756 --> 00:06:39.178
She reached behind her and took out a little toy sword and a few old rags.

99
00:06:39.959 --> 00:06:44.072
She pretended that the sword was a doll and the rags were its clothes.

100
00:06:44.873 --> 00:06:48.514
Meanwhile Eponine and Azelma had abandoned their doll.

101
00:06:49.334 --> 00:06:53.255
They had caught the cat and were busy trying to dress it in doll clothes.

102
00:06:54.115 --> 00:06:56.756
"This little girl is not your own child?"

103
00:06:57.156 --> 00:06:58.876
Valjean asked Madame Thenardier.

104
00:06:58.896 --> 00:07:02.938
"No, her mother left her with us.

105
00:07:03.818 --> 00:07:06.619
We do all we can for her, but we aren't rich.

106
00:07:07.379 --> 00:07:11.420
We haven't heard from her mother for months, so we suspect she's dead."

107
00:07:12.352 --> 00:07:17.436
Cosette overheard this conversation and said to herself, "My mother is dead!"

108
00:07:17.956 --> 00:07:21.939
But as hard as she tried, she could not remember anything about her mother.

109
00:07:23.080 --> 00:07:26.442
She darted out and brought the girls' doll back under the table.

110
00:07:27.723 --> 00:07:31.786
There she played with it for some time until Azelma noticed what was happening.

111
00:07:31.806 --> 00:07:33.987
"Mother!" she cried.

112
00:07:34.007 --> 00:07:35.288
"Look there!"

113
00:07:35.308 --> 00:07:38.550
"Cosette!" shouted Madame Thenardier.

114
00:07:38.570 --> 00:07:40.732
"Stop playing with that doll!"

115
00:07:41.636 --> 00:07:47.178
Sobbing, Cosette came out from under the table and laid the doll at Madame Thenardier's feet.

116
00:07:47.198 --> 00:07:51.139
"Why is it a problem that Cosette is playing with the doll?"

117
00:07:51.479 --> 00:07:52.239
asked Valjean.

118
00:07:52.259 --> 00:07:54.200
"The girls weren't using it."

119
00:07:54.220 --> 00:08:00.181
"That beggar dared to touch my children's doll with her horrid, dirty hands."

120
00:08:01.261 --> 00:08:05.142
Valjean walked straight to the door, opened it, and went outside.

121
00:08:05.783 --> 00:08:11.392
In a few minutes he returned with the beautiful doll from the Christmas stall.

122
00:08:11.412 --> 00:08:15.616
"Here, Cosette," he said, tenderly laying the doll in her arms.

123
00:08:16.457 --> 00:08:17.558
"This is for you."
